WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:05.000
Robotic Ricks, meta-rants, and, oh yeah, a
freakin' lightsaber?

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.918
What's next for Rick and Morty in season 7?

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:12.400
In the penultimate episode of "Rick and Morty"
Season 6, there's a bit of a change in the

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.799
multiverse's meanest scientist.

00:00:14.799 --> 00:00:18.630
After a typical shouting match at the start
of the episode when Morty accepts a sword

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:21.610
from the Knights of the Sun, Rick announces
that he's going to be

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:26.949
"I'm gonna be like, 22% more agreeable with
you for like, maybe one episode or one adventure."

00:00:26.949 --> 00:00:32.130
Morty is understandably wary of this unusual
spurt of kindness from his grandpa, and he

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:34.030
repeatedly asks what the catch is.

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:38.945
Rick assures him that there is no catch, but
in the next episode, we discover that's a lie.

00:00:38.945 --> 00:00:43.720
The Rick present in "A Rick in King Mortur's
Mort" is actually a robot created by the real

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:48.930
Rick, who has been toiling away in one of
his secret basement labs trying to track down Rick Prime.

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:53.329
He assures Morty that the robot was only present
for the one episode, and that it was Morty

00:00:53.329 --> 00:00:56.840
calling him "boring" that pushed him to make
the change.

00:00:56.840 --> 00:01:01.880
C-137 looks about as rough as he ever has
when Morty discovers him in the basement,

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:06.900
as the physical and emotional toll of hunting
his nemesis has clearly worn him down.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:11.229
The tragic part is, the whole family seems
far better off with the robot Rick.

00:01:11.229 --> 00:01:17.130
His 22% increase in love and kindness has
a profound impact on everyone's overall happiness,

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:21.705
which makes it all the more upsetting when
we learn that it was just one of Rick's self-serving tricks.

00:01:21.705 --> 00:01:25.990
The "Rick and Morty" Season 6 finale sees
the return of one of the show's most prominent

00:01:25.990 --> 00:01:29.009
side characters, U.S. President Curtis.

00:01:29.009 --> 00:01:33.299
Usually stuck somewhere between malicious
villain and incompetent fool, Curtis appears

00:01:33.299 --> 00:01:38.689
this time to avert global destruction when
Morty drops his new lightsaber at a "perfectly

00:01:38.689 --> 00:01:43.030
vertical" angle — it goes straight through
the floor and keeps on going, heading right

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:44.360
for the Earth's core.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:49.049
Curtis helps stop the lightsaber, but it soon
becomes apparent that he wanted it for himself

00:01:49.049 --> 00:01:50.049
all along.

00:01:50.049 --> 00:01:54.550
"Rick and Morty" has parodied just about every
major sci-fi franchise known to man, and it's

00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:59.399
taken plenty of digs at "Star Wars" over the
years, but the finale spends a surprising

00:01:59.399 --> 00:02:01.250
amount of time on the spoof.

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:06.079
Through Morty and the president, the writers
actually discuss the nuances of the ever-passionate

00:02:06.079 --> 00:02:07.130
"Star Wars" fandom.

00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:11.319
It's more thoughtful than most of the show's
parodies, and it reestablishes the president

00:02:11.319 --> 00:02:13.391
as a supremely silly character.

00:02:13.391 --> 00:02:14.700
"Disney ruined it!

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:17.860
You think I want 30 low-rent tv series with
bad CGI?

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:20.900
They film everything on that one big green
screen."

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:22.548
"Like you've got better ideas!"

00:02:22.548 --> 00:02:26.750
Intercut with the whole lightsaber fiasco
are some scenes of Rick doing experiments

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:27.355
in his lab.

00:02:27.355 --> 00:02:31.830
It's been a while since the Season 6 premiere,
so you'd be forgiven for not recognizing what

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:32.830
he's doing.

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:37.580
The device he analyzes is one of the attack
drones present on Rick Prime's space station,

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:40.629
which Rick and Morty visited in the Season
6 opener.

00:02:40.629 --> 00:02:45.170
Apparently, Rick acquired one of the robots
to run tests on, though it's not entirely

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:47.260
clear what information he gleans from this.

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:52.260
We also see Rick analyzing the dancing Rick
from Rick Prime's space station, who's revealed

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:56.160
in the post-credits scene of "Solaricks" to
in fact be the man himself.

00:02:56.160 --> 00:03:02.019
Whether or not Rick C-137 knows this is unclear,
but his scientific analysis of the man's bouncing

00:03:02.019 --> 00:03:03.680
butt bears fruit.

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:06.900
Through all of this, Rick almost appears to
be running on autopilot.

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:11.489
He clearly hasn't shaved or bathed in quite
some time, and it seems that his revenge quest

00:03:11.489 --> 00:03:13.276
is once again consuming him.

00:03:13.276 --> 00:03:17.398
Unfortunately, the answers he finds aren't
as simple as he'd like them to be.

00:03:17.885 --> 00:03:23.420
Using all the data collected from Rick Prime's
space station hideout, Rick C-137 is able

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:25.739
to pinpoint where the villain is.

00:03:25.739 --> 00:03:30.700
Unfortunately, his computer starts highlighting
numerous other possible locations.The confusing

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:32.700
thing here is what Rick says later.

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:37.709
When he shows Morty the multiverse scans revealing
Rick Prime's many locations, Morty asks if

00:03:37.709 --> 00:03:39.670
he's seeing every place the villain could
be.

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:40.780
"I wish, Morty.

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:42.620
It's all the places he is."

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:43.620
"Ah, jeez."

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:45.129
"Welcome to my darkness."

00:03:45.129 --> 00:03:48.860
Does this mean that Rick Prime has a bunch
of clones across the multiverse?

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:51.209
Or that he uses some kind of time travel?

00:03:51.209 --> 00:03:54.810
Or perhaps that he stays on the move and jumps
around so frequently that it's impossible

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:56.908
to ever pin down his true location?

00:03:56.908 --> 00:04:03.069
We don't find out for sure, and it's likely
that Rick C-137 himself doesn't actually know.

00:04:03.069 --> 00:04:07.200
As he tells Morty, he's spent most of his
life hunting the guy, and he's hardly any

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:08.595
closer to victory.

00:04:09.082 --> 00:04:13.349
By the end of "Rick and Morty" Season 6, the
hunt for Rick Prime is front and center.

00:04:13.349 --> 00:04:19.750
For five seasons, Rick C-137 hardly even mentioned
his vendetta against the evil doppelgänger.

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:23.850
But after getting so close to the culprit
in the Season 6 opener, Rick is back on the

00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:25.530
case in full force.

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:27.550
And this time, he's taking Morty with him.

00:04:27.550 --> 00:04:32.199
In an effort to mend fences with his grandson
after the whole robot reveal, Rick invites

00:04:32.199 --> 00:04:36.060
Morty into his lab and shows him what he's
dug up on Rick Prime.

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:41.287
He quickly becomes manic and grimly foreshadows
what may happen as they hunt the villain together.

00:04:41.287 --> 00:04:44.435
"Hunting him destroyed me, Morty, but now
we're going to do it together.

00:04:44.435 --> 00:04:45.237
You and me."

00:04:45.237 --> 00:04:45.802
"Oh, uh…"

00:04:45.802 --> 00:04:47.256
"It's going to take over your life, Morty."

00:04:47.256 --> 00:04:52.000
Despite Rick bringing Morty in on his revenge
quest at the end of Season 6, the two characters

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:53.960
still seem somewhat at odds.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:58.740
All the goodwill built up by robo-Rick's kindness
is erased when the twist of his true nature

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:03.270
is revealed, and Morty once again feels tricked
and manipulated by his grandpa.

00:05:03.270 --> 00:05:07.970
At the end of Season 5, he demanded that Rick
start treating him more like an equal, and

00:05:07.970 --> 00:05:10.030
for a while, that seemed to be going well.

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:12.140
But now, things appear to be regressing.

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:16.190
However, while Rick may be reverting to his
old ways, things aren't back to the way they

00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:17.660
originally were.

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:21.500
Morty has become more of an equal party in
their adventures over the last two seasons,

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:24.830
and that power has made it harder for Rick
to manipulate him.

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:28.560
Rick bringing him into the hunt for Rick Prime
will be a test for their relationship, and

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:32.824
it should be interesting to see how their
dynamic plays out as they pursue the villain.

00:05:33.292 --> 00:05:37.940
By the end of "Rick and Morty" Season 6, the
Smith family looks a good deal different than

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:39.910
it did at the start of the show.

00:05:39.910 --> 00:05:44.280
After a truly wild ride over the past few
years, Jerry has reached a kind of equilibrium.

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:48.910
He's still not the sharpest tool in the shed,
but he's regained some respect in the eyes

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:52.270
of his family and is far less pitiful than
he once was.

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:56.340
Of course, the biggest change in the Smith
family dynamic is the consistent presence

00:05:56.340 --> 00:06:00.389
of Space Beth, who's become a kind of cool
aunt to Morty and Summer.

00:06:00.389 --> 00:06:04.520
She's also introduced a… curious element
to Beth and Jerry's relationship.

00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:08.460
Ethics of sleeping with your clone aside,
the relationship between the three adults

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:10.490
appears to have had benefits for them all.

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:14.780
With the balance among the rest of the family
at what might be an all-time high, Rick becomes

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:15.880
the outcast.

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:20.750
His decision to replace himself with a robot
seems selfish and manipulative, but it might

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:23.539
actually suggest a greater degree of self-loathing.

00:06:23.539 --> 00:06:27.960
Rick sees that his family is happier, and
he doesn't feel like he can be a part of that

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:29.460
new, happy normal.

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:33.030
Instead of trying to get on board with the
whole happy family thing, he hides away in

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:37.550
the basement and sends a robot out in his
place, isolating himself from the people he's

00:06:37.550 --> 00:06:38.810
grown closest to.

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:42.498
"Look man, I'm sorry I've been such a dick
in the past that you think I'm doing a thing here.

00:06:42.498 --> 00:06:44.908
I'm honestly just trying to do better by you."

00:06:45.382 --> 00:06:46.500
"Are you a robot?"

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:47.158
"Morty!"

00:06:47.158 --> 00:06:50.900
It's no secret that Rick C-137 isn't a good
person.

00:06:50.900 --> 00:06:55.120
The flashbacks we get at the end of "Rick
and Morty" Season 5 don't redeem him, but

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:58.300
they do provide a lot of context for why he
is the way he is.

00:06:58.300 --> 00:07:03.220
We see how his life was torn apart by Rick
Prime, how he dedicated his life to exacting

00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:09.450
revenge, and how decades of failure and subsequent
violence transformed Rick C-137 into a cold

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:11.220
husk of his former self.

00:07:11.220 --> 00:07:15.550
At the start of "Rick and Morty," C-137 might
be at his lowest point.

00:07:15.550 --> 00:07:19.160
But as the series moves forward, he gets some
of his mojo back.

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:22.889
Unfortunately, Rick takes some backwards steps
in the Season 6 finale.

00:07:22.889 --> 00:07:27.110
The way Rick looks and talks in his underground
lab evokes his darkest moments from the early

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:28.310
years of the show.

00:07:28.310 --> 00:07:32.801
It's clear that Rick Prime's resurgence has
sent him on a spiral, and this time, there's

00:07:32.801 --> 00:07:34.435
no telling where it will lead him.

00:07:34.783 --> 00:07:39.129
Though Rick Prime's shadow looms large over
"Rick and Morty" Season 6, we still don't

00:07:39.129 --> 00:07:40.593
know much about the guy.

00:07:40.593 --> 00:07:44.430
That's probably because Rick C-137 doesn't
know that much.

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:47.650
But who actually is Rick Prime, and what does
he want?

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:52.256
It's implied that he was one of the first
Ricks, if not the first, to develop multiversal travel.

00:07:52.256 --> 00:07:54.062
His name would seem to back that up.

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:59.882
It's also clear that he's incredibly calculated
and psychotic, even beyond the levels of normal Ricks.

00:07:59.882 --> 00:08:02.602
But why did he leave his family in the first
place?

00:08:02.602 --> 00:08:07.528
Does his role as Morty's actual grandfather
have something to do with him being "the Mortiest Morty?"

00:08:07.528 --> 00:08:10.159
And what's his overall plan, if he even has
one?

00:08:10.508 --> 00:08:14.370
One character who fans may have expected to
see at the end of "Rick and Morty" Season

00:08:14.370 --> 00:08:19.509
6 is Evil Morty, the schemer who makes a dramatic
escape in the Season 5 finale.

00:08:19.509 --> 00:08:23.550
He's the reason Morty learns about Rick's
tragic backstory, and the reason his portal

00:08:23.550 --> 00:08:24.950
gun is disabled.

00:08:24.950 --> 00:08:30.099
At the end of Season 5, Evil Morty transcends
the Central Finite Curve and ventures into

00:08:30.099 --> 00:08:31.250
a new beginning.

00:08:31.250 --> 00:08:36.710
Wherever he goes, it must be far away indeed,
as there's no sign of him anywhere in Season 6.

00:08:36.710 --> 00:08:38.864
To be fair, that makes complete sense.

00:08:38.864 --> 00:08:43.370
Evil Morty's only ambition was to get away
from Ricks, so why would he come back after

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:45.150
completing that goal?

00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:49.250
It's entirely possible that his story is now
over, and that we'll never see him in the

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:50.250
show again.

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:54.790
With Rick Prime becoming the show's main antagonist,
there's less room for Evil Morty anyway.

00:08:54.790 --> 00:08:59.714
Still, it would be fun to see him pop up again
in the future, even just for a cameo.

00:08:59.826 --> 00:09:04.820
As has become standard, Mr. Poopybutthole
makes an appearance in the post-credits scene

00:09:04.820 --> 00:09:06.860
of the "Rick and Morty" Season 6 finale.

00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:12.110
In the time since we last saw him, the little
yellow guy has gotten swole, though apparently

00:09:12.110 --> 00:09:14.400
not swole enough for serious squatting.

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:17.790
Mr. Poopybutthole just can't catch a break,
it seems.

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:22.882
Since he's often shown watching the series
just like we are, he's probably in some far-off dimension.

00:09:22.882 --> 00:09:27.197
However, that doesn't mean that he couldn't
be brought back into the main story at some point.

00:09:27.197 --> 00:09:30.280
In fact, knowing "Rick and Morty," you can
probably count on it.

00:09:30.827 --> 00:09:34.089
"Rick and Morty" is going to be around for
a few more years at least.

00:09:34.089 --> 00:09:38.800
Reportedly, the team behind the show are already
at work on Season 7 and Season 8.

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:43.390
There's also a Season 9 in the pipeline, showrunner
Scott Marder told Newsweek,

00:09:53.430 --> 00:09:57.910
The Season 6 finale gives us a pretty good
idea of what the next season may entail.

00:09:57.910 --> 00:10:02.440
In the final scene of the episode, Rick flies
into one of his classic fourth-wall-breaking

00:10:02.440 --> 00:10:06.530
rants, declaring that the show's next installment
will be all about Rick Prime.

00:10:06.530 --> 00:10:09.370
"Rick and Morty Season 7: Hunting my nemesis.

00:10:09.370 --> 00:10:13.029
Maybe trying to stay healthy while doing it,
juggling plates, not every episode, Morty.

00:10:13.029 --> 00:10:15.420
It could be all happening in the background,
who knows?"

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:19.600
It's the same brand of noncommittal fan teasing
that the show has become known for, but it

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:24.110
also paints a pretty clear portrait of what
the big-picture story threads of Season 7

00:10:24.110 --> 00:10:25.110
will be.

00:10:25.110 --> 00:10:29.600
We'll probably still get mostly one-off episodes,
like Rick says, but he and Morty will also

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:32.300
be working together to hunt Rick Prime.

00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:36.930
With luck, we'll learn a bit more about him,
our own Rick and Morty, and the larger multiverse

00:10:36.930 --> 00:10:37.450
along the way.

